  "note": "An attack on a BUA in three phases: a foothold on the periphery, systematic progress within the area by bounds, reduction of individual centres of resistance (IBB S49 para 3 p 265). The frontal assault is costly: the assault comes from a flank by night, soon after dusk, the lanes in the minefield made secretly the same night or the night before; the heavy weapons sited close to the minefield neutralise the weapons on the periphery first (paras 6-10 pp 266-267). The foothold no wider than 100 m a Pl (para 15 p 268); the streets the boundaries and killing areas (para 16); adequate reserves at all levels (para 2 e p 265). Laid on the left flank attack's geometry.",
